---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Values" description="The principles behind Filthy Rich Soil Co. — soil first, craft in the detail, and the people who do the work treated as the skilled workers they are.">

<style is:global>
  .values-hero {
    position: relative;
    min-height: 60vh;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    padding: 80px 5% 80px;
    background-image: url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1464226184884-fa280b87c399?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1800&q=80');
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
    background-attachment: fixed;
  }
  .values-hero::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(to top, rgba(1,20,10,0.92) 0%, rgba(1,20,10,0.5) 55%, transparent 100%);
  }
  .values-hero .hero-content { position: relative; z-index: 1; max-width: 640px; }
  .values-hero h1 {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 5.5vw, 5rem);
    font-weight: 900; font-style: italic;
    color: #FAF7F0; line-height: 1.05; margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .values-hero p {
    font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 300;
    color: rgba(250,247,240,0.75); max-width: 500px; line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .values-body {
    background: #080e08;
    padding: 100px 5%;
  }
  .values-body-inner {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .value-block {
    padding: 60px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(184,134,11,0.15);
  }
  .value-block:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .value-num {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-style: italic;
    font-size: 3.5rem; font-weight: 900;
    color: rgba(184,134,11,0.15);
    line-height: 1; margin-bottom: 16px; display: block;
  }
  .value-block h2 {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 1.9rem; font-weight: 700;
    color: #FAF7F0; margin-bottom: 22px;
  }
  .value-block p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: rgba(250,247,240,0.65);
    line-height: 1.88; margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .value-block p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .value-em { color: #d4a017; font-weight: 500; }

  .values-quote-section {
    background: #0a140a;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(184,134,11,0.12);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(184,134,11,0.12);
    text-align: center;
    padding: 100px 5%;
  }
  .values-quote-section blockquote {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.6rem); font-weight: 400;
    color: #FAF7F0; line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto 28px;
  }
  .values-quote-section cite {
    font-size: 0.7rem; color: #B8860B;
    text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2.5px; font-style: normal;
  }

  .values-cta {
    background: #080e08;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 90px 5% 100px;
  }
  .values-cta h2 {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem,3.5vw,3rem);
    color: #FAF7F0; margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .values-cta p {
    color: rgba(250,247,240,0.6); margin-bottom: 36px;
    font-size: 1.05rem; max-width: 440px;
    margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;
  }
  .values-careers-link {
    margin-top: 28px; margin-bottom: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem !important;
  }
  .values-careers-link a {
    color: var(--gold-lite); text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(212,160,23,0.35);
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }
  .values-careers-link a:hover { border-color: var(--gold-lite); }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .values-hero { background-attachment: scroll; }
  }
</style>

<section class="values-hero">
  <div class="hero-content">
    <h1>This Work Is Guided by Principles,<br>Not Just Practices.</h1>
    <p>What drives every decision we make on your land.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="values-body">
  <div class="values-body-inner">

    <div class="value-block reveal">
      <span class="value-num">01</span>
      <h2>Soil Is the Foundation of Everything</h2>
      <p>Most landscaping companies never look below the surface. We start there. Before we touch a lawn, a bed, or a border, we test what's happening in the ground — its structure, its biology, its capacity to hold water and support life. It informs every decision we make above it.</p>
      <p>When that foundation is healthy, everything above it thrives. <span class="value-em">Most people never see the work. They just see a property that's flourishing.</span></p>
    </div>

    <div class="value-block reveal">
      <span class="value-num">02</span>
      <h2>The Craft Is in the Detail</h2>
      <p>Ecological doesn't mean unrefined. We do high-end pruning — sharp edges, deliberate lines, an eye for fullness and how a planting reads against a walkway, a wall, a roofline. The kind of work that takes years to learn to see correctly, and that most of this industry stopped teaching.</p>
      <p>And we're not anti-lawn. A well-placed lawn is one of the most effective tools for keeping invasive species at bay across a large property — and it's where your kids play, where the dog runs, where Saturday mornings happen. <span class="value-em">We just don't think a lawn needs to be the entire property to do its job.</span> A lawn with purpose, bordered by native plantings and healthy soil, is a lawn that actually makes sense.</p>
      <p>The ecology tells us what to plant and where. <span class="value-em">The craft is what makes it look exactly right.</span></p>
    </div>

    <div class="value-block reveal">
      <span class="value-num">03</span>
      <h2>The Person Tending the Soil Matters as Much as the Soil</h2>
      <p>Land care used to be a skilled trade. Much of the industry now runs on the opposite idea — crews hired cheap, taught nothing, worked until they're used up, and replaced. Properties suffer for it, because the person on your land is the one making the hundred small decisions that add up to whether it thrives.</p>
      <p>We keep a small crew and we develop it. People are trained on real properties, given a real path forward, and kept. <span class="value-em">The same faces every visit is not a courtesy. It's how the work gets good.</span></p>
    </div>

    <div class="value-block reveal">
      <span class="value-num">04</span>
      <h2>Biodiversity Is Not a Trend</h2>
      <p><span class="value-em">A diverse system regulates itself.</span> Multiple species, layered canopies, native plants that co-evolved with this landscape — they build on each other season after season. Monoculture lawns work the opposite way. They depend on the next application to hold their appearance — and the moment that stops, so does the result. Diversity breaks that dependency.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="value-block reveal">
      <span class="value-num">05</span>
      <h2>Your Property Should Need Less Every Year</h2>
      <p>The longer we work a property, the better we know it. We learn where water moves, where soil needs support, where the right plant in the right place saves three interventions a season. That knowledge compounds, and the property gets easier to keep well — not harder.</p>
      <p>That is the opposite of how most land care is sold. A program built on synthetic inputs has to be repeated forever, because nothing underneath ever actually gets fixed. <span class="value-em">Ours is built to make itself less necessary.</span></p>
    </div>

    <div class="value-block reveal">
      <span class="value-num">06</span>
      <h2>We're In It for the Long Run</h2>
      <p>A stewardship relationship isn't a contract — it's a commitment. We're invested in what your property becomes over years, not just what it looks like after the first season. The work we do today is designed to matter in ten years.</p>
      <p>That's why we document everything — soil numbers, photographs, what worked and what took longer than we expected. <span class="value-em">The land we tend is the legacy we leave, and we intend to be able to show it.</span></p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="values-quote-section">
  <blockquote class="reveal">"Land isn't a backdrop. It's a living system — and we're responsible for what happens to it while it's in our care."</blockquote>
  <cite>— Filthy Rich Soil Co.</cite>
</section>

<section class="values-cta">
  <h2>See our values in the ground</h2>
  <p>Start with a walk around your property. We'll tell you honestly what we see.</p>
  <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Request a Walkthrough</a>
  <p class="values-careers-link">Believe in this work? <a href="/careers">We're hiring one Apprentice Steward for 2027 →</a></p>
</section>

</Base>
